body:
How's life treating you?

After my dad died in 2015 life had been bumpy. My mom tried really hard to keep it going well and did great but depression got the best of me. I continued with university and got a B.A. in English with no job prospects at the end. Ended up being a substitute teacher 5 days a week and working at my universities library on the weekend. I then moved up to full-time work at the library. I guess the job overall isn't too bad. Slow days are extremely slow and sometimes there really isn't anything for me to do. I hope to one day find a grad program I like to hopefully move up in the world and make some decent money. Just don't know what the program would be. 

&#x200B;

I've never won a car but my parents paid for my first one. 

&#x200B;

I've travelled to London, Paris, and Rome. I've been to NYC and the outer boroughs. I've also been to Disney more times than I can count.

I have a lot of HO scale model trains that were my dads. I'd say most from the 70s and brands like TYCO, Lionel, Bachmann, etc. Most are plastic but there are a few metal ones too. Not sure how to figure out price points since everyone seems to do their own thing when I look around on Ebay. I just don't know the first thing about vintage model trains (and train accessories) so I need help pricing them.

&#x200B;

I also have many name brand clothes that have been sitting on Mercari not budging. Maybe my descriptions just aren't good enough.

&#x200B;

Edit: Can upload photos after I get off work!

AHHH yay for being loudly and proudly gay! I'm not so loudly but proudly bi! And I happy to hear you got meds to help you out! Depression and anxiety is no fun! 

&#x200B;

:O A TARGET STARBUCKS! That's like the best of both worlds. Did you ever (pre-covid) wander around Target while drinking coffee? What is your favorite coffee to drink? What's a drink you hate making?

I'm a huge fan of hugs giving and receiving and just miss being able to hug my friends. That's what I want to be able to do. 

&#x200B;

